#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md:6
msgid "`to`: Non-consuming Conversion"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md:8
msgid ""
"Prefix to a function that takes a borrowed value and creates an owned value"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md:11
msgid "// Copyright 2025 Google LLC\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md:12
msgid "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md:21
msgid "// Take an owned self because `u32` implements `Copy`\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md:28
msgid ""
"Methods that create a new owned value without consuming `self`, and imply a "
"type conversion, are named starting with `to`."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md:31
msgid ""
"Methods that start with \"to\" return a different type, and strongly imply a "
"non-trivial type conversion, or even a data transformation. For example, "
"`str::to_uppercase`."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md:35
msgid ""
"\"to\" methods most commonly take `&self`. However they can take `self` by "
"value if the type implements `Copy`: this also ensures that the conversion "
"method call does not consume `self`."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md:39
msgid ""
"If you simply want to define a method that takes `&self` and returns an "
"owned value of the same type, implement [`Clone`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/"
"stable/std/clone/trait.Clone.html) or [`ToOwned`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/"
"stable/std/borrow/trait.ToOwned.html)."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md:42
msgid ""
"If you want to define a method that consumes the source value, use the "
"\"into\" naming pattern."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md:45
msgid ""
"Also seen in functions that convert the endianness of primitives, or copy "
"and expose the value of a newtype."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md:51
msgid "More to Explore"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md:53
msgid ""
"Ask the class: What's the difference between `to_owned` and `into_owned`?"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md:55
msgid ""
"Answer: `to_owned` appears on reference values like `&str`, whereas "
"`into_owned` appears on owned values that hold reference types, like `Cow` "
"(copy-on-write)."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/to.md:59
msgid ""
"Types like `Cow` can be owned while containing references that are borrowed, "
"so the owned value of `Cow` is consumed to create an owned value of the "
"reference type it was holding onto."
msgstr ""
